WEBVTT

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.380
Oh!

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.790
The city tournament has finally begun!

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:12.990
We, the Momoyama Predators, faced the Yabusawa Eleven in our second match.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.830
Even I scored in that match, and we won!

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.930
Our next match is the semifinals.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.500
We're going up against Aoto-kun's team, the Heavenly!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.670
Aoto!

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.570
That's the kid who scored all of their goals.{That's the one. He scored all of their goals.}

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:07.810
From back then...

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.850
What's wrong with him?

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.620
It's because he met Aoto-kun.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.120
Oh yeah, last year...

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.090
Yeah.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:31.300
We did beat the Heavenly, but 
Aoto-kun scored all three of their goals.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.930
Kota-kun didn't like that at all.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:38.400
So he lost his own personal matchup, eh?

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.340
Is he that good?

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.840
Well, you'll see when you watch him play.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.410
My dad should've filmed it.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:48.450
Did you?

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:49.720
Of course.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.250
If you want to see it, I'll burn a DVD for you.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.350
Please do.{Thank you very much.}

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.390
We're facing the Heavenly during the semifinals!

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.690
You look happy.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.090
Well, yeah.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:05.460
I told you before how the Heavenly's 
coach didn't want any girls on his team.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.170
I have to pay him back for that!

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.270
You're right.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:12.100
You kept looking at Aoto-kun.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.110
Did something happen?

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.610
N-No, it's nothing.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:16.640
What?

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.940
What are you talking about?

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.410
Nothing at all.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:23.120
In any case, we must beat the Heavenly!

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:28.320
Everyone! We're aiming to conquer the entire nation!

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.220
We must beat the Heavenly!

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.620
Oh!

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:34.930
I'm so full!

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.130
That was delicious!

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.930
Is it someone's birthday?

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.400
Nope, it's no one's birthday.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.400
But it says "Congratulations."

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.240
It's to celebrate Shou's first goal!

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.070
Oh! Is that so?

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.950
You get cake all because of your big bro!

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.210
Thank me!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.520
Yes, yes. Look at that bruise on your face. Good job.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.120
At least give me something positive.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.420
Shou, congratulations on your first goal!

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:03.860
Thank you!

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.760
Cheers!

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.460
How do you feel about your first goal?

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.530
The best!{Awesome!}

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:16.500
Thank goodness I kept on playing soccer!

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.240
Then keep that feeling into the semifinals.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:22.610
Work hard and score lots of goals, okay?

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.510
Y-Yeah...

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.610
That's what I want to do...

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:27.750
What's wrong?

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.310
He has no confidence.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.620
No!

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.420
The next match is not one where I'm going to score goals.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.060
There's a striker named Aoto-kun.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.420
I need to work hard on the defense.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:40.630
Oh?

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:44.200
I must stop him, no matter what.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.170
What kind of team are they?

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.770
The Kawahara International Heavenly.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:53.010
They're an international school, so 
a lot of their players are foreigners.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.070
Oh?

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.070
Foreigners, eh?

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.880
Then you're representing Japan, Shou.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.480
That sounds kinda cool.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.270
Why are you avoiding his pass, Ouzou-kun?

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.170
I can't help it.

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.210
His pass seems painful if I receive it head-on.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:32.140
Ouzou-kun, I know it's early in the morning, but I want you to be more serious.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.980
My body's not awake yet.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.720
There's not much use in practicing something new right now.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:41.220
Is it okay for you to say that?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.560
Jeez.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:49.700
I know how badly you want to beat Aoto, but 
don't get so heated up so early in the morning.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.730
I can't win if I'm not fired up.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:54.070
Let's just roll with it like we did last year.

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:56.400
Was it fun winning like that?

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.950
We triple-teamed him. I can't call that a win.{I can't say we beat him by triple-teaming him.}

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.720
That's soccer, too.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.090
A win is a win, no matter how you do it.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.060
Are you serious?

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:24.660
I find it annoying sometimes that we share the same DNA.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:27.270
Me too.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:29.740
Oh well.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.240
I get it.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.980
The triplets sealed Aoto-kun last year?

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:46.390
Heavenly was a team where Aoto-kun was the focal point.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:48.450
We just needed to stop him.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.260
But it's different this year?

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.590
Well... I think it's pretty much the same.

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:56.700
The problem lies with the Furuyas.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.560
They're going to be selfish and play on their own again?

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:04.040
Especially Kota-kun. He sees Aoto-kun as his rival.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.510
I don't think he'll come back on defense.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:09.610
He wants a straight-on fight.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:10.780
Yes.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.310
Then we have to stop him this year.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.850
Yeah...

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:20.820
That guy's ball control is quite something.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:27.990
Yes.

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:33.070
We finally shut him down when the triplets teamed up on him.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:37.000
In any case, we must find a way to stop him.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.670
If we watch their match video, we might find something.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:44.110
I want to see it!

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:46.310
Well, it's not like there's a special reason or anything.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.180
What's wrong?

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.480
Over there...

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:58.260
Kyoko-san and the Furuyas' father.

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:02.190
Looks like they're happily chatting.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.960
What are they talking about?

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.530
I-I think this is like a development for a shady drama.

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.170
Erika-chan.

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:12.040
Oh? Lunchboxes from the convenience store?

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:14.470
They don't contain enough nutrients.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:17.180
But they're delicious.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:21.880
What are you guys doing?

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:24.850
A match video DVD of Aoto-kun's match?

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.220
Yep.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.220
I asked Furuyas' dad to flim it.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:31.020
I met him here to get a copy.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.530
We made a copy for you guys, too. Want to see it?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.930
Of course!

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.330
Thank you very much!

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:40.970
You're welcome.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:43.570
Do your best in the semis.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.600
I'll be going now.

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:48.610
Oh, Kyoko-san.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:52.740
You should try cooking yourself. Later.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.710
Oh, okay.

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:10.960
What are you doing?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.030
O-Ow.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:16.200
I think having lunchboxes from the 
convenience store isn't giving you enough nutrients.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.500
I want to try cooking today.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:22.370
You can cook?

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.340
How rude.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:27.580
Just shut up and go watch your match.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.880
O-Okay.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.820
The ball reaches Aoto-kun again!

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.060
Wow!

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:46.870
He passed three guys in an instant!

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.800
Wow...

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.010
What an easy goal.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.810
Is it that easy to score a goal?

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:00.780
He's so cool.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:04.120
He's pretty good.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.500
I see now.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.900
H-H-Hot!

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.530
That's weird.

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:28.900
What's wrong?

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:31.040
Their goalkeeper changed.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.240
Their goalkeeper?

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:36.470
Last year, Heavenly had a much better goalkeeper.

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:37.880
What happened to him?

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.340
Is he injured?

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.380
Maybe.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:44.320
But, without that keeper, we're at a great advantage.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:47.790
You're right, but Aoto-kun is too good.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:51.560
It's like the ball sticks to his legs.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:55.230
But it seems like he doesn't run back to defend.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.900
He never passes, either.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:12:00.400
Yeah. All he's interested in is scoring goals.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.430
He does everything by himself.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:07.440
If we want to beat the Heavenly, we must stop Aoto-kun.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:10.310
No matter how good he is, as 
long as we keep three guys on him,

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.310
he'll lose the ball sooner or later.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:15.680
I can't do that.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:18.150
There must be a way.

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:20.350
If we notice his quirks and weaknesses,

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.450
we can figure something out.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:23.820
Let's watch this one more time.

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:24.990
Okay!

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:49.250
Masaru-chan. Masaru-chan!

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.790
You are still watching that match?
 Is this the fourth time? The fifth time?

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.050
Do you know how late it is?

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:58.220
Aren't you hungry?

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:00.630
Oh, it's this late already?

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.130
I'm hungry.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.630
I already finished eating.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.730
Eh? Weren't you going to cook?

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:11.600
What are you talking about?

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:16.040
In any case, is Aoto-kun's match that interesting?

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.840
It interests me, I can tell you that much.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.350
That guy is a pure striker.

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:22.850
His ball control is quite good.

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:27.420
It's like, "Float like a butterfly, sting like a bee."

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.250
Of course Kota sees him as a rival.

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:32.060
This semifinal match just got a lot more interesting.

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:33.990
How's the miso soup?

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:35.030
Aren't you gonna drink it?

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:37.230
Oh.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:41.370
So sour!

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:43.700
What is this terrible miso soup?

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.300
Where did you buy this?

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.210
Don't buy this brand anymore.

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:49.510
I'm going home!

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:53.010
You only care about soccer, Masaru-chan!

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.010
Eh?

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:56.580
Hey!

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:57.680
You can take care of the rest.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:58.850
Wait!

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.890
What are you talking about?

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:35.950
So have you figured out a way to stop Aoto?

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:41.760
Well... I couldn't figure anything out just by watching the DVD!

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:42.990
Eh!?

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:46.300
What? Then we can't do anything?

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:48.830
No, I think there's something we can take advantage of.

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:52.270
They have a different goalkeeper this year.

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:54.970
Aoto-kun! Our match is finally here!

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:58.480
Are you nervous?

00:14:58.480 --> 00:14:59.280
Yes.

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:00.950
This morning, Papa said...

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:07.920
"Reika, even Shou-kun scored. I want you to score, too."

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.660
He told me that. It's impossible.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:13.630
Don't say that!

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:15.760
You can score, too!

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:19.130
No way. It's impossible for me.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:22.630
No! No! Don't give up!

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.040
Just think that you can do it!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.000
You can do it!

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.670
Right, Reika-chan?

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:29.470
Thank you!

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:32.940
I'm giving today's match my all!

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:36.820
Kota, there's no point in being so pumped up right now.

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:39.280
Yo.

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:42.190
We meet if you win one more match.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:45.490
I've been waiting for this day.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:47.660
How nice of you.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:51.360
But Heavenly has Aoto-kun.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.430
Even I admit that he's a genius striker.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.470
So what?

00:15:56.940 --> 00:16:01.110
You finally stopped him last year by triple-teaming him.

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:03.680
I don't think he'll fall for the same thing this year.

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:07.980
I want to tell you his weakness.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.410
Hey, hey.

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:11.780
I appreciate the thought,

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.790
but mind your own business.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:14.720
What he said.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:16.650
Is that okay?

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:19.490
I'm telling you not to do anything unnecessary.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:25.200
Kageura, before you worry about other
 people, can you even win your own match?

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:26.930
That's right.

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:31.840
We've decided to conquer the entire
 nation even without you worrying about us.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.810
That's how it is.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:35.310
I see.

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:37.210
Then I'll wait for good results.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:42.250
We went to Spain to train recently.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:44.450
What does that have to do with us?

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:49.750
We played international youth teams
 from Europe, South America, and Asia.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:50.560
So?

00:16:50.890 --> 00:16:52.360
Of course, we won.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.890
I see.

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:56.900
However, we aim to become number one in the galaxy.

00:16:56.900 --> 00:17:00.330
The galaxy? Wow, that's amazing.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:01.970
Well, I get it.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.770
See you in the finals.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.910
He's still an annoying guy.

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:10.910
Hey! Furuyas!

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:18.880
Our match against the Kawahara
 International Heavenly is in one hour.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:22.320
After watching the DVD of their last match,

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:24.460
it's just like what the Furuyas said.

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:28.430
Aoto on the Heavenly is a very tricky striker.

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:31.360
Here is our strategy for this match.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.260
No guard, all offense.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.770
No guard, all offense?

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:39.840
Isn't that boxing?

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:41.770
Sounds painful.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.780
I'm just making an analogy.

00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:48.580
Defense is important, but this 
match is going to be all about offense.

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:55.050
#11 Aoto is very strong, but the Heavenly defense is pretty weak.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.520
If we get scored on, then just get those goals back.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:00.430
Just play with that thought and you can win!

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:01.390
Okay!

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:03.630
Yes! Here we go!

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:11.140
Tagi.

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:14.570
I'm here. You're going against the triplet demons today, right?

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:15.310
Yep.

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:18.110
You lost against them last year. I guess this is a grudge match?

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.850
Do you have a plan?

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:23.350
Not really.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:27.750
The coach has some ideas, but all I have to do is score.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.320
That's just like you.

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:30.720
Well, do your best.

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:33.190
I'll be cheering you on.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.970
Hmm? What's wrong?

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:44.200
Coach, I think going back and forth on offense is all right,

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.770
but what should Reika-chan and I do?

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:50.710
What do you need before you can go on offense?

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:54.150
Before you can go on offense...

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.510
First you need to get the ball.

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:58.520
That's right.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:01.550
Then don't be afraid and challenge for the ball.

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:04.390
We won't be able to stop Aoto easily,

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:09.160
but when Ouzou and Erika fail to stop him, you should step up and stop him.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:11.830
When you get the ball, press forward.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:15.230
Then score like you did last time.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:18.000
Eh? Can I do that?

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.500
Of course!

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:21.110
Reika, you too!

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:22.910
Eh? Me too?

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:25.210
Okay!

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.150
Aoto-kun.

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:40.690
Hey, you can't tell us apart?

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:42.090
What do you want?

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:43.360
What's wrong, Aoto?

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.030
Are you okay?

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:48.330
No problem. We're just greeting him before the match.

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:51.270
There's no problem. I'm fine.

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:58.240
We won't be triple-teaming 
you like last year, so don't worry.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:02.250
We don't want to be seen as bullying a little kid.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:06.850
I don't care either way. It won't be like last year.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:09.950
Oh well.

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:12.990
Let's have a good match. Right, Kota-kun?

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:14.060
Yeah.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:24.670
Onii-chan!

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.410
Honey, we've got to hurry. The match is starting.

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.410
Yes, yes, I understand.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:45.260
Okay! Nice expressions on all of you.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:47.690
Go out there with no guard and all offense!

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:48.790
Yes!

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:52.260
We are the Momoyama Predators!

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:53.730
We aim to be...

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.170
...number one in the galaxy!

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:56.270
Okay!

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:59.140
We'll just keep on scoring today!

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:01.310
Oh!

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:03.980
Go! Shou!

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:05.540
Go, Onii-chan!

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:09.310
I see. Your cooking plan failed, huh?

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:14.620
Yeah! Masaru-chan just thinks about the Predators now.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:16.390
He doesn't even care about me anymore.

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:22.190
That's not true! Masaru-chan-san thinks about you a lot.

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.690
Really?

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:25.400
That's right.

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:29.730
Masaru-chan-san is just bad at expressing his feelings.

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:31.740
Then that's good.

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:33.200
Oh, it's starting.

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:56.090
Crap!

00:21:56.090 --> 00:21:57.900
Aoto-kun, let's go!

00:22:08.540 --> 00:22:10.540
I won't let you pass!

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:48.780
He passed by seven players...

00:24:35.020 --> 00:24:37.050
Seven players!? He's too good!

00:24:37.050 --> 00:24:39.390
Ouzou-kun! Everyone! Calm down!

00:24:39.390 --> 00:24:41.660
We have to pay them back!

00:24:41.660 --> 00:24:45.030
Kota-kun's all caught up in being his rival! What do we do?

00:24:45.030 --> 00:24:48.700
Remember our brand of soccer! There must be a way!

00:24:48.700 --> 00:24:51.100
I'll stop Aoto-kun! Just you wait!

00:24:51.570 --> 00:24:53.300
Next episode of Ginga e Kickoff!!

00:24:53.300 --> 00:24:54.870
No Guard.
